    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0523" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg237"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2599</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-19T13:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 19, 1916, 1 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 20, 3 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3769. Informed by newspaper correspondent that Zimmermann told him yesterday that Germany would make no further
                    concessions in submarine war. Zimmermann, according to McClure, read and approved the manifesto given to McClure and cabled you—my 3754,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d309-f1"/> April 16, 4 p. m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
